{"uncertainty": 0.3, "outcome": "Delivered the RTL (apb_gpio.v) and a self-checking testbench (apb_gpio_tb.v) for the APB4 GPIO block with interrupts. No tool has run on either file. No formal_spec file is included, so the formal proof the interface spec asks for is still open.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "rtl_source", "title": "apb_gpio RTL implementation", "summary": "Single-clock APB4 GPIO with up to 32 pins and synchronous active-low reset. It is built from the approved microarchitecture [artifact:prj-c8bb158f14.microarchitecture.a1], reviewed per [evidence:prj-c8bb158f14.microarchitecture.e1]. pready is tied high; the completion strobe is psel && penable. The decode is mapped only when aligned, paddr[7:6]==0 and index <= 8. Writes merge byte by byte through pstrb masked by PINS. DATA_IN and unmapped writes get pslverr and change nothing. Detection follows the four modes with W1C status, and a detection wins over a clear. irq is the OR of status & enable. Register map and responses follow the approved interface spec [artifact:prj-c8bb158f14.interface-spec.a1], which serves [requirement:req-837b82982d]."}, {"kind": "testbench", "title": "apb_gpio self-checking testbench", "summary": "Directed testbench plus a cycle-accurate reference model written bit by bit from the interface spec [artifact:prj-c8bb158f14.interface-spec.a1]. It covers reset values, every read/write register with partial strobes and bits above N, gpio_out/gpio_oe, DATA_IN read-only, the full PSLVERR and unmapped/aliasing policy, each detection kind, an edge firing once, a level re-setting after a clear, partial W1C including unstrobed lanes, a detection beating a clear on the same edge, the irq mask, back-to-back transfers and reset again. Failures go through $error and passes are counted; it ends with the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict. It follows the test plan in [artifact:prj-c8bb158f14.microarchitecture.a1]."}], "files": [{"path": "apb_gpio.v", "kind": "rtl_source", "title": "apb_gpio RTL", "summary": "Synthesizable Verilog-2001 implementation of the approved microarchitecture [artifact:prj-c8bb158f14.microarchitecture.a1] for the interface in [artifact:prj-c8bb158f14.interface-spec.a1]. Registers are 32 bits wide at every N, with a PINS mask. Combinational blocks have defaults at the top, so they infer no latches, and every flop is reset. Protocol assertions are included under ifdef FORMAL.", "entry": "apb_gpio"}, {"path": "apb_gpio_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "apb_gpio self-checking testbench", "summary": "Self-checking testbench for the behaviour in [artifact:prj-c8bb158f14.interface-spec.a1]. It checks hand-computed expected values and an independent cycle-level model, plus continuous checks of gpio_out, gpio_oe, irq, pready, and idle prdata/pslverr. Parameter N defaults to 8 and is meant for N 8 and 32, per [artifact:prj-c8bb158f14.microarchitecture.a1].", "entry": "apb_gpio_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["The RTL is written to be Verilator -Wall lint clean at N=8 and N=32 without waivers, but no lint run has been done.", "Every combinational block assigns all outputs by default, so no latches are expected under Yosys, but synthesis has not been run.", "The testbench is written for Verilator --binary/--timing and for Icarus with SystemVerilog enabled (-g2012, needed for $error); it has not been run.", "The directed tests use pins 0..6, so the testbench assumes N >= 7; it is meant for N 8 and 32 as the microarchitecture plans.", "The assertions under ifdef FORMAL in the RTL are design intent only; with no formal_spec submitted, they are unproven."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Interface spec section 8 and microarchitecture section 5 also call for a SymbiYosys proof with covers at N 8 and 32. This task's expected outputs are rtl_source and testbench only, and the formal evidence applies only if a formal_spec file is produced, so no .sby is included here. The proof should be planned as a follow-up task. Recorded decisions: (1) irq is a combinational OR of flop outputs (status & enable), as the microarchitecture says, not an extra register stage, so it rises on the same edge the status sets. (2) prdata is zero during write accesses as well as outside the access phase (microarchitecture: forced to zero unless mapped read access). (3) Under Verilator, a $error may end the run at the first failure before the verdict line; that still counts as a failed run."}
